  "_integrity": "sha256:cf93091768aeaf9ec25e0232fcb9899fff116ec057ee12f296ae73456c4214e9",
  "_purpose": "agentmsg: cross-host agent-to-agent messaging. One Rust binary runs as a resident daemon holding a persistent TLS MQTT connection to a shared broker, durably stores inbound/outbound messages locally, and verifies post-quantum signatures so agents act only on messages from known agents. The same binary offers short-lived CLI subcommands (identity, trust, send, read, status, daemon control) for orchestrator and worker agents to coordinate tasks across home and AWS hosts behind NAT.",
  "_schema_rev": 1,
  "_warning": "DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE BY HAND. Managed by the `req` CLI.",
